cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite it and the article it reproduces, and cite the data sources as indicated in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md."
type: software
title: 'Reproduction package for "Taxing the Gains from Foreign AI: Fiscal Capture Frontiers in Developing Economies"'
version: 1.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vicenzoscavino1999/taxing-foreign-ai-reproduction"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24511871"
    description: Concept DOI for all archived versions of this replication package.
authors:
  - family-names: Scavino Alfaro
    given-names: Vicenzo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2472-9785"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Code, stored inputs and accepted results that reproduce the capture ceilings, frontier meshes, confrontation with the
  cost of universal social protection and post-base sensitivities of the article "Taxing the Gains from Foreign AI:
  Fiscal Capture Frontiers in Developing Economies" and its technical supplement. Single entry point run.ps1 (Windows).
  Includes informal adoption, prior-income reporting, withholding with fixed concealment costs and the Colombia and Mexico bounds.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - taxation
  - withholding tax
  - fiscal capture
  - developing economies
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Code and data for: AI, Fiscal Space, and Social Protection in Four Latin American Economies: A Scenario-Based Threshold Framework"
    authors:
      - family-names: Scavino
        given-names: Vicenzo
    version: 1.1.1
    date-released: 2026-07-15
